@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain

-- g4-registrar.l4: Law 5785-2025, section 19: the Registrar's appointment, consent and recognition powers.
-- Group G4 (the Registrar and the Council), written by ENCODER G4.  Source: inputs/law.wiki, cited as src:N
-- (quotation lines are copied from that file by script, work/g4/build.py), checked against the gazette
-- (Sefer HaChukim 3349, p. 186).  English beside the Hebrew is the encoder's paraphrase; the Hebrew governs.
--
-- What this module takes as INPUT (the standard names of phase1/PLAN.md section (c), exact):
--   `the Council was consulted`, `the Council's advice was validly given`  (IP7; decided by g4-council-work),
--   and the Registrar's opinions as fields named `in the Registrar's opinion ...` (IP17).
-- What it exports for the INTEGRATOR to wire (IP5): `s 19(b) — the study programme has the Registrar's consent`,
--   `s 19(b) — the study programme satisfies the requirement of the Registrar's consent` and
--   `s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)`.
-- Imports only prelude and domain: no date is counted in s.19, so the time module is not imported.
-- A discretion of the Registrar is an input; a duty or power is a regulative rule typed by who acts and what is done.
-- The performer check of the language fires on a constant act and on a trace event, not on an enum constructor
-- inside a rule, so every regulative rule below is traced in g4-tests-registrar.l4 with its own PARTY as performer.

§ `Chapter 4: the Registrar and the Council`

§§ `Section 19: appointment of the Registrar and the Registrar's powers`

§§§ `The acts of this section, and the facts it asks about`

-- One action type for the whole section.  The first actor-typed field is the performer, so a trace
-- event by anyone else is refused by the language.
DECLARE `An act under section 19` IS ONE OF
    `appoint a person to hold the Registrar's powers` HAS
        actor IS A Party
        `the appointee` IS A STRING
        `the appointee is an employee of the Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `publish notice of the appointment of the Registrar in Reshumot` HAS
        actor IS A Party
        `the appointee` IS A STRING
    `give the Registrar's consent to a study programme` HAS
        actor IS A Party
        `the programme` IS A STRING
    `recognise a certificate, degree or training from a foreign educational institution` HAS
        actor IS A Party
        `the qualification` IS A STRING
    `make a recognition conditional` HAS
        actor IS A Party
        `the qualification` IS A STRING
        `the condition` IS A `Condition of a recognition under section 19(c)(2)`
    `consider the level of the foreign studies` HAS
        actor IS A Party
        `the qualification` IS A STRING
    `consider the programme of the foreign studies` HAS
        actor IS A Party
        `the qualification` IS A STRING
    `consider the scope of the foreign studies` HAS
        actor IS A Party
        `the qualification` IS A STRING
    `consider the duration of the foreign studies` HAS
        actor IS A Party
        `the qualification` IS A STRING

-- s.19(c)(2): "בעמידה במבחן מקצועי או בלימודי הכשרה או בשניהם, לפי העניין": a test, training studies, or both, as the case may be.
DECLARE `Condition of a recognition under section 19(c)(2)` IS ONE OF
    `passing a professional test`
    `completing training studies`
    `both passing a professional test and completing training studies`

@desc The facts about one appointment of a Registrar that s.19(a) asks about
DECLARE `Appointment of a Registrar` HAS
    `the Minister appointed the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person was appointed by the Minister of Labour
    `the person is an employee of the Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person is an employee of the Ministry of Labour (the appointment is to be made from among them)
    `notice of the appointment was published in Reshumot` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if notice of the appointment was published in Reshumot

@desc A study programme, including a course of complementary studies, and the facts s.19(b) asks about
DECLARE `Study programme under section 19(b)` HAS
    `the programme` IS A STRING @desc The name of the study programme
    `a final certificate as stated in section 6(a)(4) can be obtained through the programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a final certificate of the kind s.6(a)(4) speaks of can be obtained through the programme
    `the Registrar consented to the programme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar gave consent to the programme

@desc A certificate, degree or training from a foreign educational institution and the facts s.19(c) asks about
DECLARE `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` HAS
    `a description of the qualification` IS A STRING @desc What the certificate, degree or training is
    `a certificate, degree or training from an educational institution in a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if it is a certificate, degree or training from an educational institution in a country other than Israel
    `in the Registrar's opinion the scope and content of the studies match the training requirements of section 6(a)(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc The Registrar's opinion ("אם ראה"): an input, never computed
    `the Registrar recognised the qualification as meeting the training and examination requirements for a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar recognised it
    `the Registrar made the recognition conditional on a test, training or both` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the recognition was made conditional under s.19(c)(2)
    `the condition of the recognition was met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the person met the condition the Registrar set (read only where the recognition was made conditional)

@desc The matters s.19(c)(2) says the Registrar considers, as a record of what the Registrar did
DECLARE `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` HAS
    `the level of the studies, compared with the level customary at institutions the Training Division recognises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar considered it
    `the programme of the studies, compared with the programme customary at institutions the Training Division recognises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar considered it
    `the scope of the studies, compared with the scope customary at institutions the Training Division recognises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar considered it
    `the duration of the studies, compared with the duration customary at institutions the Training Division recognises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar considered it

§§§ `Section 19(a): the Minister appoints the Registrar`

-- src:160 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} השר ימנה, מקרב עובדי המשרד, אדם שיהיו נתונות לו סמכויות הרשם לפי חוק זה; הודעה על מינוי הרשם תפורסם ברשומות.
@ref s.19(a) (src:160)
GIVEN appointment IS AN `Appointment of a Registrar`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(a) — the person was appointed to hold the Registrar's powers` appointment MEANS
        appointment's `the Minister appointed the person`
    AND appointment's `the person is an employee of the Ministry`

-- FORK F-19a: publication is not a condition of the appointment.  The text makes the notice a duty that follows
-- ("הודעה על מינוי הרשם תפורסם ברשומות") and s.2 defines the Registrar as "מי שמונה לפי סעיף 19": one who was
-- appointed, not one whose appointment was published.  The alternative is a callable function.
@ref s.19(a) (src:160)
GIVEN appointment IS AN `Appointment of a Registrar`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(a), alternative reading — the appointment counts only once notice of it was published` appointment MEANS
        `s 19(a) — the person was appointed to hold the Registrar's powers` appointment
    AND appointment's `notice of the appointment was published in Reshumot`

-- The duty ("ימנה": shall appoint) names no time, so the rule has no WITHIN.  Only an appointment of a person who is
-- an employee of the Ministry (the last field is TRUE) is performance of it.  The duty to publish follows it:
-- the sentence "תפורסם" names no actor (FORK F-19a-actor); the Minister, who appoints, is taken as the actor.
@ref s.19(a) (src:160)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 19`
`s 19(a) — the Minister must appoint, from among the Ministry's employees, a person to hold the Registrar's powers` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MUST `appoint a person to hold the Registrar's powers` `the Minister` appointee TRUE
    HENCE (
        PARTY `the Minister`
        MUST `publish notice of the appointment of the Registrar in Reshumot` `the Minister` appointee
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "s 19(a): notice of the appointment of the Registrar was not published in Reshumot"
    )
    LEST BREACH BY `the Minister` BECAUSE "s 19(a): no person was appointed to hold the Registrar's powers from among the Ministry's employees"

-- FORK F-19a-actor, alternative: the Ministry (the body whose employee the Registrar is) is the one that must publish.
@ref s.19(a) (src:160)
GIVEN appointee IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 19`
`s 19(a), alternative reading — the Ministry must publish notice of the appointment of the Registrar in Reshumot` appointee MEANS
    PARTY `the Ministry`
    MUST `publish notice of the appointment of the Registrar in Reshumot` `the Ministry` appointee
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Ministry` BECAUSE "s 19(a): notice of the appointment of the Registrar was not published in Reshumot"

§§§ `Section 19(b): the Registrar's consent to a study programme`

-- src:161 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} תוכנית לימודים, לרבות לימודי השלמה, שניתן בשלהם לקבל תעודת גמר כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|בסעיף 6(א)(4)}}, טעונים את הסכמת הרשם.
@ref s.19(b) (src:161)
GIVEN programme IS A `Study programme under section 19(b)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(b) — the study programme needs the Registrar's consent` programme MEANS
    programme's `a final certificate as stated in section 6(a)(4) can be obtained through the programme`

@ref s.19(b) (src:161)
@export The Registrar has given consent to this study programme (IP5: the programme was approved by the Registrar)
GIVEN programme IS A `Study programme under section 19(b)` @desc The study programme and whether the Registrar consented to it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(b) — the study programme has the Registrar's consent` programme MEANS
    programme's `the Registrar consented to the programme`

-- "טעונים את הסכמת הרשם": programmes that lead to a final certificate need the consent; others do not.
@ref s.19(b) (src:161)
@export Whether a study programme satisfies the requirement of the Registrar's consent: it is met where the programme does not need the consent or has it
GIVEN programme IS A `Study programme under section 19(b)` @desc The study programme, whether a final certificate of the s.6(a)(4) kind can be obtained through it, and whether the Registrar consented
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(b) — the study programme satisfies the requirement of the Registrar's consent` programme MEANS
        (NOT `s 19(b) — the study programme needs the Registrar's consent` programme)
    OR  `s 19(b) — the study programme has the Registrar's consent` programme

-- The consent is the Registrar's act and the Registrar's discretion: the power is a MAY, and it arises only for a programme that needs it.
@ref s.19(b) (src:161)
GIVEN programme IS A `Study programme under section 19(b)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 19`
`s 19(b) — the Registrar may give consent to the study programme` programme MEANS
    IF   `s 19(b) — the study programme needs the Registrar's consent` programme
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `give the Registrar's consent to a study programme` `the Registrar` (programme's `the programme`)
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Section 19(c)(1): recognition of a foreign certificate, degree or training`

-- src:162 | {{ח:תת|(ג)|(1)}} הרשם, לאחר התייעצות עם המועצה, רשאי להכיר בתעודה, בתואר או בהכשרה ממוסד לימודים במדינת חוץ כעמידה בדרישות הכשרה ובבחינות הנדרשות לשם קבלת רישיון, אם ראה שהיקף הלימודים ותוכנם תואמים את דרישות ההכשרה כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|בסעיף 6(א)(4)}}.
-- FORK F-19c-advice: "לאחר התייעצות עם המועצה" (after consulting the Council).  Reading taken: the Council was consulted
-- AND its advice was validly given (s.24 to s.26, decided in g4-council-work, wired by the INTEGRATOR): a "consultation" of a
-- body that could not lawfully give advice is not a consultation of the Council.  The alternative asks only that the Council was consulted.
-- The Registrar is not BOUND by the content of the advice: only that it was sought and validly given.
@ref s.19(c)(1) (src:162)
@export Whether the Registrar may recognise a foreign certificate, degree or training as meeting the training and examination requirements for a licence
GIVEN qualification IS A `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` @desc The foreign certificate, degree or training and the Registrar's opinion on its scope and content
      `the Council was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar consulted the Council before deciding (IP7)
      `the Council's advice was validly given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Council's advice was validly given under sections 24 to 26 (IP7)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` qualification `the Council was consulted` `the Council's advice was validly given` MEANS
        qualification's `a certificate, degree or training from an educational institution in a foreign country`
    AND `the Council was consulted`
    AND `the Council's advice was validly given`
    AND qualification's `in the Registrar's opinion the scope and content of the studies match the training requirements of section 6(a)(4)`

@ref s.19(c)(1) (src:162)
GIVEN qualification IS A `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)`
      `the Council was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(c)(1), alternative reading — a foreign qualification may be recognised once the Council was consulted` qualification `the Council was consulted` MEANS
        qualification's `a certificate, degree or training from an educational institution in a foreign country`
    AND `the Council was consulted`
    AND qualification's `in the Registrar's opinion the scope and content of the studies match the training requirements of section 6(a)(4)`

@ref s.19(c)(1) (src:162)
GIVEN qualification IS A `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)`
      `the Council was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Council's advice was validly given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 19`
`s 19(c)(1) — the Registrar may recognise the foreign qualification` qualification `the Council was consulted` `the Council's advice was validly given` MEANS
    IF   `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` qualification `the Council was consulted` `the Council's advice was validly given`
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `recognise a certificate, degree or training from a foreign educational institution` `the Registrar` (qualification's `a description of the qualification`)
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Section 19(c)(2): what the Registrar considers, and the power to attach a condition`

-- src:163 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} בהחלטה כאמור בפסקה (1) ישקול הרשם, בין השאר, את רמת הלימודים, את תוכנית הלימודים, את היקף הלימודים ואת משך הלימודים במוסד לימודים במדינת חוץ, בהשוואה לרמת הלימודים, לתוכנית הלימודים, להיקף הלימודים ולמשך הלימודים הנהוגים במוסדות לימוד מוכרים על ידי האגף להכשרה מקצועית; הרשם רשאי להתנות הכרה כאמור בעמידה במבחן מקצועי או בלימודי הכשרה או בשניהם, לפי העניין.
-- "ישקול הרשם, בין השאר": the Registrar considers the four matters AMONG OTHERS, so the four are a minimum, not a closed list.
-- The duty is four acts the Registrar must each do, in parallel (RAND); no time is stated, so no WITHIN.
@ref s.19(c)(2) (src:163)
GIVEN qualification IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 19`
`s 19(c)(2) — in a decision to recognise, the Registrar must consider the level, programme, scope and duration of the studies` qualification MEANS
        (PARTY `the Registrar`
         MUST `consider the level of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` qualification
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar` BECAUSE "s 19(c)(2): the level of the studies was not considered")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the Registrar`
         MUST `consider the programme of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` qualification
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar` BECAUSE "s 19(c)(2): the programme of the studies was not considered")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the Registrar`
         MUST `consider the scope of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` qualification
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar` BECAUSE "s 19(c)(2): the scope of the studies was not considered")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the Registrar`
         MUST `consider the duration of the foreign studies` `the Registrar` qualification
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the Registrar` BECAUSE "s 19(c)(2): the duration of the studies was not considered")

-- The same duty read off a record of what the Registrar did.
@ref s.19(c)(2) (src:163)
GIVEN matters IS A `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar considered the level, programme, scope and duration of the studies` matters MEANS
        matters's `the level of the studies, compared with the level customary at institutions the Training Division recognises`
    AND matters's `the programme of the studies, compared with the programme customary at institutions the Training Division recognises`
    AND matters's `the scope of the studies, compared with the scope customary at institutions the Training Division recognises`
    AND matters's `the duration of the studies, compared with the duration customary at institutions the Training Division recognises`

-- "הרשם רשאי להתנות הכרה כאמור": a power, exercised case by case ("לפי העניין"), so which condition is a wildcard.
-- It arises only where the Registrar may recognise (s.19(c)(1)).
@ref s.19(c)(2) (src:163)
GIVEN qualification IS A `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)`
      `the Council was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Council's advice was validly given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `An act under section 19`
`s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar may make the recognition conditional on a test, training or both` qualification `the Council was consulted` `the Council's advice was validly given` MEANS
    IF   `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` qualification `the Council was consulted` `the Council's advice was validly given`
    THEN PARTY `the Registrar`
         MAY `make a recognition conditional` `the Registrar` (qualification's `a description of the qualification`) condition
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The consequence for IP5: a recognition counts (for G2, s.6(a)(4)) when the Registrar did recognise, was entitled to under (c)(1),
-- considered the four matters of (c)(2), and, if the recognition was conditional, the condition was met.
-- src:162 | {{ח:תת|(ג)|(1)}} הרשם, לאחר התייעצות עם המועצה, רשאי להכיר בתעודה, בתואר או בהכשרה ממוסד לימודים במדינת חוץ כעמידה בדרישות הכשרה ובבחינות הנדרשות לשם קבלת רישיון, אם ראה שהיקף הלימודים ותוכנם תואמים את דרישות ההכשרה כאמור {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 6|בסעיף 6(א)(4)}}.
-- src:163 | {{ח:תתת|(2)}} בהחלטה כאמור בפסקה (1) ישקול הרשם, בין השאר, את רמת הלימודים, את תוכנית הלימודים, את היקף הלימודים ואת משך הלימודים במוסד לימודים במדינת חוץ, בהשוואה לרמת הלימודים, לתוכנית הלימודים, להיקף הלימודים ולמשך הלימודים הנהוגים במוסדות לימוד מוכרים על ידי האגף להכשרה מקצועית; הרשם רשאי להתנות הכרה כאמור בעמידה במבחן מקצועי או בלימודי הכשרה או בשניהם, לפי העניין.
@ref s.19(c) (src:162-163)
@export Whether a foreign qualification was recognised in accordance with section 19(c): the Registrar recognised it, was entitled to, considered the four matters, and any condition set was met
GIVEN qualification IS A `Foreign qualification under section 19(c)` @desc The foreign qualification, the Registrar's opinion, and whether the Registrar recognised it and on what condition
      matters IS A `Matters the Registrar considered under section 19(c)(2)` @desc What the Registrar considered
      `the Council was consulted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Registrar consulted the Council (IP7)
      `the Council's advice was validly given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Council's advice was validly given under sections 24 to 26 (IP7)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 19(c) — the foreign qualification was recognised under section 19(c)` qualification matters `the Council was consulted` `the Council's advice was validly given` MEANS
        qualification's `the Registrar recognised the qualification as meeting the training and examination requirements for a licence`
    AND `s 19(c)(1) — a foreign qualification may be recognised` qualification `the Council was consulted` `the Council's advice was validly given`
    AND `s 19(c)(2) — the Registrar considered the level, programme, scope and duration of the studies` matters
    AND (   (NOT qualification's `the Registrar made the recognition conditional on a test, training or both`)
         OR qualification's `the condition of the recognition was met`)
